      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Authors studied the occurrence and clinical outcome of hiatal hernia in 18 patients during a 7-year period. The age of the children from 10 years to 15 years, with a mean age of 12.8 years. Their patients had recurrent abdominal pain, 4 of them had chest pain. 13 patients had macroscopic oesophagitis. Under medically treatment 16 patients has been well. Two cases required surgery. Aetiology of hiatal hernia in children is unknown."},
